Nephi schrieb:
> It has been proposed many times that mirrors should provide
> reflection. Of course, given the prevalence of nymphs, that would be
> unbalancing. But it seems to me that if a wielded mirror gave
> reflection, but shattered after a single use (or perhaps had a
> significant chance of shattering after each use), game balance would
> be maintained. It would give games a little more flavor, I think.

I think a mirror should reflect _without breaking_, as long as the
mirror is _explicitly wielded_. In practise that bears the danger
of hitting a monster with the wielded mirror by accident (thereby
imposing a severe luck penalty). A handicap is that you first have
to wield it in case of breath/ray attacks, usually (in case of rays)
suffering from the first hit anyway, and switch again to your melee
weapon (thus risking being zapped again, as long as the wand isn't
empty) or giving you a chance to flee; I find this a quite balanced
response to the mostly inevitable deadly wand attacks in the early
game; you suffer, but you have a chance to survive (for the moment).

